Z||000000||DjKid||08-25-2000||02:58 PM||||Okey, this car is beginning to drive me nuts.. I get one thing fixed and something else flips out on me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> First thoughts is, short in my headlight/driving light circut.. cuz everytime I turn my driving lights on, the fuse blows ... instantly.. Somethings mucked up <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I've searched everywhere for a short, my question is, seeing how I am not electric inclind, could a relay or something be bad causing it to blow the fuses instantly, it first started it when I was trying to turn my head lights on and they wouldn't go up, so I turned em off and back on real quick.. blown fuse..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> HELP! please?<P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||11
Z||000001||DjKid||08-25-2000||03:00 PM||||Forgot to mention, brake lights, backup lights, turn signals all work fine... ugh <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||08-25-2000||04:09 PM||||It may be your headlight controller module. This is INSIDE the drivers side fender in front of the wheel. Remove the screws that hold the wheel liner on and the screws behind the side marker light. You should be able to If reach it and pull the connector off of it. Pull the one that has the most wires(5 or 6), that is the input side. The output side has 4 wires.<BR>Replace the fuse and turn on the switch. It could be shorted and causing the fuse to blow. These are not cheap from new sources but junk 87-91 firebirds have them. The module says "GUIDE" on it.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DjKid||08-25-2000||04:22 PM||||Is this unit the same on all years? I got a 87 parts car.. would it work on my 88?<P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||08-25-2000||05:45 PM||||87 an 88 modules are the same.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Thor||08-26-2000||11:56 PM||||OK you and I have the very same problem on my 86GT which I'v posted at this forum a week and a half or so ago under [headlight/tailight problem]...What I know for sure so far is that I have a short accuring in my taillight wireing rearward of the firewall.  I know this because I had a chance to work a bit on this vexing problem today. This is what I did...First put a fresh 20amp fuse in. Removed all the rear bulbs. Turned the parking lights on and WHAM !. Blew the fuse. Turned the lights off. Then I removed the rear grill over the battery to inspect a large wireing loom connector for anything obveous [Located attached to the frame just above and rearward of the battery]. Then I disconected the connecter. You do this by removing a bolt located in the middle of the face of the connecter. Then I put in a fresh fuse and turned the parking lights on...Hey! the fuse did'nt blow...So now I know It was'nt a bad bulb and It's in the parkinglight/license plate wireing. I don't have a proper 86 manual[I have an 84 GM]but I believe the connecter name is C500.<BR>I'm going to spend an hour or so on this problem again tommarow and I promise you I'll post you my results!  Let me know if you discover anything the same or different.<BR> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Thor (edited 08-27-2000).]||||reg||3
